From 5751bd3e8626cb77dcd05d2335a710302a4084b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:52:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(security): harden auth and configuration, resolve lint
 errors

Security
- Refuse to start outside development with the dev/placeholder/short
  SECRET_KEY, DEBUG=true, or wildcard CORS origins
- Enable CORS middleware using CORS_ORIGINS (was configured but unused)
- Use the user ID as the JWT subject; require exp and sub claims
- Equalize login timing for unknown accounts; rate limit failed logins
  (HTTP 429, in-memory, per process)
- Reject unknown fields on register/login so role cannot be supplied
- Handle concurrent duplicate registration (409 instead of 500)
- Add require_roles() dependency for role-restricted endpoints
- Add security response headers; serve API docs only in development
- /health returns 503 when the database is unreachable
- Docker image runs as non-root with a health check; CI read-only perms

Quality
- Fix all ruff errors (imports, B008, BLE001, UP017, F401, E501) and
  enable E,F,I,B,UP,BLE rules
- Replace deprecated on_event with lifespan
- Ignore *.egg-info/, build/, dist/
- Expand tests from 3 to 25; update docs/SECURITY.md

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011VarDJrPNNxiobdRVsj4gK
