 # Security baseline
 
-Keep secrets outside source control and replace the development JWT secret before deployment. Passwords are hashed with Argon2 through pwdlib. Public registration only assigns the farmer role; privileged roles require a separate administrative process. Add authorization and organization isolation to every protected business endpoint as those modules are introduced. Use HTTPS, trusted CORS origins, upload validation, authentication rate limits, backups and tested restoration. Never log passwords or bearer tokens.
+## Implemented
+- Passwords are hashed with Argon2 through pwdlib. Login does equal work for unknown accounts to limit timing-based account discovery.
+- JWT bearer tokens (HS256) carry the user ID, require `exp` and `sub`, and are rejected when the user is missing or deactivated.
+- The app refuses to start outside development with the built-in dev secret, a placeholder or short (<32 character) `SECRET_KEY`, `DEBUG=true`, or a wildcard in `CORS_ORIGINS`.
+- Public registration only assigns the farmer role and rejects unknown fields such as `role`. Privileged roles require a separate administrative process. `require_roles(...)` guards role-restricted endpoints.
+- Failed logins are rate limited per client address and email (default 5 per 15 minutes, then HTTP 429). The limiter is in memory and per process; use a shared store such as Redis when running several workers or replicas.
+- CORS allows only the origins in `CORS_ORIGINS`. Responses carry `X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options` and `Referrer-Policy`, and `/api/` responses are `Cache-Control: no-store`. Interactive API docs are served only in development.
+- `/health` returns HTTP 503 when the database is unreachable. The container runs as a non-root user with a health check, and CI runs with read-only repository permissions.
 
-This initial baseline is not a completed security audit.
+## Still to do
+- Keep secrets outside source control and generate a unique `SECRET_KEY` for every deployment.
+- Add authorization and organization isolation to every protected business endpoint as those modules are introduced.
+- Use HTTPS, upload validation, database migrations, backups and tested restoration. When running behind a reverse proxy, make client IP detection trust only that proxy.
+- Never log passwords or bearer tokens.
+
+This baseline is not a completed security audit.
